WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.388
A context window is the amount of text, instructions, conversation history, retrieved content, examples, and tool output a model can consider during a request.

00:00:10.388 --> 00:00:15.157
It is the working space the model has available when producing an answer.

00:00:15.157 --> 00:00:29.661
Everything placed into that space competes for attention: system instructions, developer instructions, user requests, prior messages, documents, summaries, code, citations, and the output the model is expected to generate.

00:00:29.661 --> 00:00:32.340
Context is measured in tokens, not words.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:40.114
A token can be a whole word, part of a word, punctuation, spacing, or another text fragment depending on the tokenizer.

00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:49.914
The exact conversion varies, but the engineering point is simple: every instruction, document, example, and response consumes part of a finite budget.

00:00:49.914 --> 00:00:58.016
Output tokens matter too, because a request that fills the entire input space may leave too little room for a useful answer.

00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:05.725
Large context windows change workflows because they let teams include more source material before asking for analysis.

00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:12.650
A model can review longer documents, more code, richer chat history, or larger sets of retrieved evidence.

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:19.118
That does not mean the model understands everything equally well or that structure stops mattering.

00:01:19.118 --> 00:01:25.325
More room helps only when the information is relevant, organized, and clearly tied to the task.

00:01:25.325 --> 00:01:28.461
Context management is an engineering discipline.

00:01:28.461 --> 00:01:40.482
It involves deciding what to include, what to summarize, how to order material, how to label sources, how to preserve provenance, and how to prevent noise from burying important facts.

00:01:40.482 --> 00:01:42.769
The goal is not to fill the window.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:48.322
The goal is to give the model the right information in a form it can use effectively.
